WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.450
- This episode of Legal Eagle

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.120
was made possible by Skillshare.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.880
Learn to think like a lawyer for free

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.290
for two months by clicking on
the link in the description.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.740
Usually claiming this is
a constitutional crisis

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.130
in this administration is just hyperbole,

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.140
but something was different
when the administration

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.440
attempted to include
a citizenship question

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.790
in the American census.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.020
The Supreme Court has
already answered that query

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.840
with a big fat no, that 2020 census

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.210
cannot include the citizenship
question on the census.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.650
And the government's lawyers
told the lawyer courts

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.870
that they were prepared to comply

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.730
with the Supreme Court's order,

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.240
until president Trump
tweeted that actually

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.890
as leader of the US government,

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.220
he might just use that question anyway.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.870
And behold, we have
what might be considered

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.670
a constitutional crisis on our hands.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.470
Can a president defy or
ignore Supreme Court order?

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.180
Has this ever happened before?

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.200
And are we out of the
woods when it comes to

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.110
a constitutional crisis?

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.470
That's what we're gonna talk about today

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.155
on this real law review.

00:00:57.155 --> 00:00:59.905
(dramatic music)

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.070
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.700
Since the day president Donald Trump

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.860
took the oath of office,
people have been predicting

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.331
a constitutional crisis.

00:01:09.331 --> 00:01:11.660
The constitution doesn't
define anything like

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.800
a constitutional crisis,
it's basically just a term

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.000
that we come up with
when we have to suggest

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.810
lots of danger when it
comes to the interplay

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.700
between different branches
of the US government.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.450
But a constitutional crisis
over whether one branch

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.200
of the US government would
acknowledge the full authority

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.570
of another is a kind of a
big deal in its own right,

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.640
and that's pretty much where we are today.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:34.000
It appears that we may
be safe for the moment,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.760
but it's worth doing a full retrospective

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.150
on the census controversy,
because things keep getting

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.240
weirder and we're not
out of the woods yet.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.480
So how did we get here?

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.760
First, a primer on the American census.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.440
The census requires
the government to count

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.180
the population of the United
States every 10 years.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.170
Counting the population
includes all people,

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.030
whether citizens or non-citizens.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.270
The census is mandated by the constitution

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.080
in Article 1, which
governs Congress's power.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.096
The Constitution requires
a census every 10 years.

00:02:01.096 --> 00:02:03.690
Congress delegates that power
to the executive branch,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.440
but it is a constitutionally-mandated
congressional power.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.410
The question of who to
include in the census

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.050
goes back to the founding of this country

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.370
and the infamous 3/5ths compromise.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.520
At the time, the southern
states, which had huge

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.920
populations of slaves,
wanted to count those

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.690
when it came to
congressional representation,

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.530
while the northern states
felt that that was unfair

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.080
because all of these
slaves were not considered

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.864
US citizens, so for better or worse,

00:02:27.864 --> 00:02:30.970
the states reached the
infamous 3/5ths compromise.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.120
The census is used to
allocate federal funds,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.360
draw legislative districts,

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.410
and reapportion congressional seats.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:39.130
Although the census once
included a citizenship question,

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.790
the Census Bureau dropped
the question in the 1950s

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.710
because it caused an under
count of the actual population.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.550
According to Census Bureau experts,

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.760
the citizenship question
scares people who live

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.000
in households that include non-citizens.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.090
Census responses are supposed
to remain confidential

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.200
and cannot be given to
any other federal agencies

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.390
to assist deportations, but many people

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.730
simply don't know or
believe that their answers

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.120
will be kept confidential,

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.500
and including the question
can be particularly

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.530
intimidating to immigrants.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.430
Some studies have shown that including

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.690
the citizenship question
reduces the actual response

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.810
rate among households with
a least one non-citizen

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.700
by as much as eight percentage points,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.550
and that is a pretty big deal.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.430
The ultimate goal of including
the citizenship question,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.299
as explained by republican
strategist Thomas Hofeller,

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:25.630
is to allow republicans to create heavily

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.730
gerrymandered maps where
likely democratic voters

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.460
are stuffed into geographically
small urban districts.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.230
Although Hofeller passed
away, his correspondence

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.840
indicated that he wanted
to use citizen population

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.930
instead of total population
to draw legislative districts,

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.750
which in his words, quote,
would be advantageous

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.970
to republicans and non-Hispanic whites,

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.120
and would dilute the
political power of Hispanics.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.350
According to the New York Times,

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.660
Hofeller wrote to Trump
and other republicans

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.950
even before the president was inaugurated

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.140
urging the Trump administration to include

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.750
the census question and
obfuscate the reason

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.410
for including it, claiming
that it was necessary

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.800
to enforce the Voting Rights Act.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.810
Once president Trump was inaugurated,

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.430
he followed Hofeller's blueprint,

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.410
and despite arguing in
court that the question

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.290
was meant to enforce
minority voting rights,

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.770
in public, Trump admitted
that that was not,

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:15.770
in fact, correct.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.983
The real reason, well
president Trump stated.

00:04:17.983 --> 00:04:20.232
- You need it for
Congress for districting.

00:04:20.232 --> 00:04:22.466
You need it for appropriations.

00:04:22.466 --> 00:04:23.717
Where are the funds going?

00:04:23.717 --> 00:04:25.127
How many people are there?

00:04:25.127 --> 00:04:27.764
Are they citizens, are they not citizens?

00:04:27.764 --> 00:04:29.480
You need it for many reasons.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:30.820
- In other words, you need it to do

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.300
precisely what Hofeller said,

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.940
to create an under count that would help

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.800
republicans and hurt democrats.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.500
Several states sued the federal government

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.360
after the Trump administration
announced it would

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.420
use the census to ask people
if they were US citizens.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.540
As those cases wound their
way through the federal court

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.090
system, the Trump administration didn't do

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.820
a particularly good job of coming up

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.890
with a facially neutral reason
for including the question.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.440
And in fact, although
Hofeller died a few years ago,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.870
his daughter discovered
documents on his hard drive

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.930
that showed the citizenship
question was designed

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.400
for the purpose of giving
white voters more power.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.970
While it's not 100% clear,
it is entirely possible

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.660
that the Supreme Court used that evidence

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.550
to determine that the Trump
administration's reasoning

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:12.130
for including the question
was in fact pretextual.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.640
So the Supreme Court said that Trump

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.310
and Labor Secretary Ross
could not put the question

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.640
on the 2020 census, and in fact,

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.630
I covered that case in the round-up

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.850
of Supreme Court cases from
this term linked below.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.650
Now during the litigation,
the government had

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.270
repeatedly told the
courts that they needed

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.640
to print census forms
no later than June 30th.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.410
That rationale allowed them to skip

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.190
the intermediate appeals court entirely

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:35.710
and go straight to the Supreme Court.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.130
The Supreme Court's decision
happened shortly before

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.030
that deadline, so when
the Supreme Court remanded

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:44.160
the case back down to
the lower federal courts,

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.180
the Department of Justice
attorneys responsible

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.740
for arguing the government's position

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.620
told the courts that the
cases were basically over

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.510
and that the government
would print the census

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:55.430
by June 30th as scheduled,
without question.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.560
Now normally that would be the
end of this particular story,

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.330
at least until the next
census in 10 years,

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:03.500
but president Trump had other ideas.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.790
Quote, so important for our
country that the very simple

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.680
and basic are you a citizen
of the United States

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.830
question be allowed to be
asked in the 2020 census.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.110
Department of Commerce
and Department of Justice

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.390
are working very hard on this,
even on the fourth of July.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:20.230
DOJ lawyers were caught
flat-footed by this tweet,

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:23.220
and in fact federal
court Judge George Hazel,

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.370
who is presiding over one
of the two census questions

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.520
in the US district for Maryland,

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.750
said that he followed Trump on Twitter

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.360
and hauled all of the
lawyers, both the plaintiffs

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.690
and the DOJ defense
lawyers, into his court

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:40.040
for an emergency conference
with all of the attorneys.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.640
In the court conference,
Judge Hazel said that

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.820
he follows president Trump on Twitter,

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:47.040
and that the tweet, quote,
directly contradicted

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.740
the position that the DOJ
had taken 48 hours earlier.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.240
The transcript of this
particular conference

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.360
is pretty remarkable,
even for a layperson.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:58.010
I would never want to
be on the receiving end

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.150
of the vitriol that Judge Hazel issued

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.110
towards the DOJ lawyers, and believe me,

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.970
contradicting something
that you have promised

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.460
to a judge is definitely not a position

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.730
that any lawyer ever wants to take.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.060
But DOJ lawyer Joshua Gardner had to tell

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:13.777
the federal court judge "the
tweet this morning was the

00:07:13.777 --> 00:07:17.150
"first I'd heard of the president's
position on this issue."

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:19.410
In other words, Gardner had no idea

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.007
what his boss was going to do or say

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:24.000
with the government's new position.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.170
Later that same day, the
lawyers had the unenviable task

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.700
of telling judges in
all of the pending cases

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.140
that all of the stuff he had said earlier

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.110
about printing the forms on July 30th

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.630
and obeying the Supreme Court, well,

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:38.020
they were basically
trying to take that back.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.570
So could president Trump
really defy an order

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:43.270
from the Supreme Court?

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.260
Well the framers of the
Constitution believed strongly

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:47.740
in checks and balances,
building a system of governance

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:49.490
where the three branches of government

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.380
constantly have the
ability to stop each other

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.850
from gaining too much power,

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:56.240
and in the famous 1803
Marbury versus Madison,

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.410
the Supreme Court
established a legal doctrine

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.500
known as judicial review, which is ability

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:03.910
of the court to declare
legislative or executive acts

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.870
in violation of the Constitution.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.820
Now judicial review was
controversial at the time,

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.370
since it's not explicitly
found in the Constitution.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.810
However, it has basically
been the law of the land

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.660
ever since 1803.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.970
At the time, Alexander
Hamilton wrote that, quote,

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.400
the courts were designed
to be an intermediate body

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.930
between the people and
the legislature in order,

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:25.450
among other things, to keep
the latter within the limits

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:27.450
assigned to their authority.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.860
James Madison once said
that an independent judicial

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.840
system provided, quote,
an impenetrable bulwark

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.410
against every assumption of power

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.570
in the legislative or executive.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.420
And so as time went on, the
Supreme Court got the final say

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.370
over whether a law was
constitutional or not.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.530
There's actually nothing
that can force the president

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:47.003
to follow the orders of the Supreme Court.

00:08:47.003 --> 00:08:49.472
The court system doesn't have an army,

00:08:49.472 --> 00:08:51.810
it really doesn't have any police officers

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.910
except for a few marshals who basically

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.200
are just there for the
protection of the judges.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.590
Judicial review is one
of the strongest norms

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:01.040
in the American government,
but presidents have

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.240
ignored Supreme Court decisions before.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:04.980
Let's start with the first real example

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.900
of a president defying the Supreme Court,

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.950
Andrew Jackson and the Cherokees.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.500
Ever since the Revolutionary War,

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:12.230
the United States had
openly desired to take

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:15.600
Cherokee and Creek land in
what is now the American south,

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.500
and Georgia had claimed
over 100 million acres

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.420
of Cherokee land as its own.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.510
The federal government
originally backed the tribes

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:24.220
and signed treaties
guaranteeing that they would

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:26.880
never have to move,
treaties that the government

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.930
would finally break when
President Andrew Jackson

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:31.010
came along and signed
the Indian Removal Act,

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.890
which aimed to force
Cherokees off their land.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:35.820
The Cherokee government
argued that they had

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:37.450
the same rights as any sovereign nation

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.300
and therefore passed a law restricting

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.880
white Europeans from
residing on Cherokee land.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.870
The ensuing court case wound
up before the Supreme Court,

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.747
which ruled for the Cherokee nation.

00:09:46.747 --> 00:09:48.870
Chief Justice John Marshall wrote that

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.400
the Cherokee had sovereignty,

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.010
which included the same
rights of possession

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:53.970
as any other nation over its own land.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.590
The court reasoned that the
tribe could exclude people

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.590
from buying its land or residing there.

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:01.482
President Jackson, however,
had very different ideas.

00:10:01.482 --> 00:10:03.407
President Jackson supposedly said

00:10:03.407 --> 00:10:05.087
"John Marshall has made his decision,

00:10:05.087 --> 00:10:06.620
"now let him enforce it."

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.530
Georgia decided to simply ignore
the Supreme Court's order,

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:11.550
and President Jackson
proceeded to let Georgia

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.170
do what it wanted, and that is how

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.950
the Cherokee ended up
leaving Georgia for Oklahoma

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.660
on a journey that is known
as the Trail of Tears.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.650
By refusing to do anything to enforce

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.310
the Supreme Court's decision,
President Jackson was

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.141
daring the court to intervene,

00:10:25.141 --> 00:10:27.520
knowing that the court's
enforcement mechanisms

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.530
were shaky at best, and
at times in the past,

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:33.630
the court had ordered federal
marshals to enforce orders,

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.190
but there isn't really any
constitutional authority

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.740
allowing for this.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:40.240
The US Marshalls work
for the Attorney General.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.390
The Attorney General is part
of the executive branch,

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:44.410
so the Supreme Court
couldn't send in the marshals

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.640
even if they wanted to.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.290
In a different case, one
of the biggest stains

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:50.260
on Abraham Lincoln's presidency
was when he suspended

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.560
the writ of habeas corpus
during the Civil War.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.000
A writ of habeas corpus
is a legal term that means

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.950
that every person in prison has a right

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:00.000
to petition the courts
for his or her release.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.540
Habeas corpus is actually
a right that is enumerated

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.510
in the Constitution, but
Lincoln suspended habeas corpus

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:08.240
rights early in the Civil War,
preferring to hold prisoners

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.700
without any mechanism for their release.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.530
The Supreme Court held
that what Lincoln did

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:14.583
was in fact unconstitutional,

00:11:14.583 --> 00:11:16.830
but President Lincoln ignored the order

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.460
because he was more worried
about the war itself.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.210
And again, there was
nothing the Supreme Court

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:24.427
could do because its orders
are not self-executing.

00:11:24.427 --> 00:11:26.580
This means that the court
doesn't have any ability

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.470
to enforce its own orders.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:31.420
In reality, the Supreme Court
and other federal courts

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.540
have to depend on the executive branch

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.100
to enforce their orders

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:38.210
since the executive is responsible
for enforcing the laws,

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.360
and the vast majority of
presidents have viewed it

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.520
as their constitutional duty
to obey Supreme Court rulings,

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:45.050
and even enforce them.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.950
When the Supreme Court
held that states could not

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:50.020
maintain an education system
that was separate but equal,

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.670
the governor of Arkansas
resisted racial integration,

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.270
but at that time,
President Dwight Eisenhower

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.180
used his authority to call on the military

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.730
to enforce the Supreme
Court's integration order.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.250
President Eisenhower said
whenever normal agencies

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:04.590
prove inadequate to the
task, it becomes necessary

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.820
for the executive branch
of the federal government

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:09.998
to use its powers and authority
to uphold federal courts.

00:12:09.998 --> 00:12:14.530
- The president's
responsibility is inescapable.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:17.150
In accordance with that responsibility,

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:20.143
I have today issued an executive order

00:12:20.143 --> 00:12:23.714
directing the use of troops
under federal authority

00:12:23.714 --> 00:12:27.082
to aid in the execution of federal law

00:12:27.082 --> 00:12:29.460
at Little Rock, Arkansas.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.190
- The National Guard went to Little Rock

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:33.680
to help make sure that
the Little Rock Nine,

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:36.010
as they were known, were
allowed to go to school,

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:38.550
enforcing Brown versus Board of Education.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.990
Most of the time, presidents
will sharply criticize

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:43.100
Supreme Court decisions,
but they will still

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:44.680
follow the court's orders.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.920
This was the case in 2004,
when Supreme Court struck down

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:50.570
president George W. Bush's
plan to have prisoners

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:53.610
held in Guantanamo Bay
tried by military tribunals

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:54.980
rather than the court system.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:59.253
Similarly in 2010, President
Obama sharply criticized

00:12:59.253 --> 00:13:02.010
the Citizens United case, but still,

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.610
President Obama did not decline to follow

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.220
the opinion as laid out
by the Supreme Court,

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.000
nor did he issue an executive order

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.840
imposing a new campaign
finance system unilaterally.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.830
It's common for politicians
to have an opinion

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.350
about whether cases are
wrongly decided or not,

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.260
but it is not normal in modern times

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:20.720
for presidents to ignore
Supreme Court orders,

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.750
which brings us to the
current administration.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.960
Did the founders leave
us totally and completely

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.910
unable to defend ourselves
against a president

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.490
who won't obey a court order?

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.470
Well, the founders of America created

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:32.390
three co-equal branches of government,

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.280
and gave the legislative branch the duty

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:36.440
to impeach a president who commits both

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:38.120
quote, high crimes and misdemeanors.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.020
Now, defining high crimes and misdemeanors

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.700
is beyond the scope of this video,

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.330
but there are plenty of
constitutional scholars

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.480
who believe that it is Congress's duty

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.090
to impeach a president who
refuses to follow the law

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:52.340
or refuses to follow
Supreme Court precedent.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:55.110
Now president Trump tends to
tweet about a lot of things

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.830
that make him angry, and
often fails to follow through

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.530
with some of the things
that he states via Twitter,

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:02.810
and it's possible that census
tweets from the president

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:03.920
are just another example of

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.810
saying one thing and doing another.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:08.250
But here, president Trump
first took to Twitter

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.810
to trash the Supreme Court's ruling,

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.990
and then said he would consider using

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.120
an executive order to add
the census question by fiat,

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.360
ignoring the Supreme Court, he said.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:19.364
- We're thinking about doing
that, it's one of the ways,

00:14:19.364 --> 00:14:21.493
we have four or five ways we could do it.

00:14:21.493 --> 00:14:22.985
It's one of the ways that we're thinking

00:14:22.985 --> 00:14:24.140
about doing it very seriously.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.380
- President Trump followed
up his comments with tweets

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.500
announcing that he would
make another announcement

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.720
about the census question
during a right-wing

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.150
social media gathering at the White House.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:35.240
Quote, the White House
will be hosting a very big

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.670
and very important social
media summit today.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.870
Would I have become president
without social media?

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:42.020
Yes, probably, at its conclusion,

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.900
we will all go to the
beautiful rose garden

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.890
for a news conference on
the census and citizenship.

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:48.740
However, after days of criticism,

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.026
during the news conference,
president Trump backed down

00:14:51.026 --> 00:14:53.610
with AG Barr stating
that the administration

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:56.070
would not be adding a
census question after all.

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:58.120
Attorney General Barr
offered his interpretation

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.400
of the Supreme Court's decision

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.620
and the legality of the
citizenship question,

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.770
said that the administration
never considered

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.030
adding that question at all.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.670
At the end of the news conference,

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.370
Attorney General Barr accused the media

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:10.720
of being hysterical by
stating that Trump would use

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.440
an executive order to usurp
the Supreme Court when

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.495
the administration had never,
ever considered doing that.

00:15:16.495 --> 00:15:19.150
- Some in the media have been suggesting

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:22.230
in the hysterical mode of the day

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.490
that the administration
has been planning to add

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:27.309
the citizenship question to the census

00:15:27.309 --> 00:15:31.933
by executive fiat without
regard to contrary court orders

00:15:31.933 --> 00:15:34.572
or what the Supreme Court might say.

00:15:34.572 --> 00:15:39.198
This has been based on rank
speculation and nothing more.

00:15:39.198 --> 00:15:42.313
As should be obvious,
there has never been,

00:15:42.313 --> 00:15:45.450
this has never been under consideration.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:46.880
- I don't really know how to square

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.660
this statement with reality.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.020
The president said exactly
the opposite of this

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:53.740
and the news media was
relying on the tweets

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:57.280
and actual verbal statements
that the president made,

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:59.130
including a question and answer

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.250
from a reporter to president Trump.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.207
The reporter asked "are you going to issue

00:16:03.207 --> 00:16:05.090
"an executive order on the census?"

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.857
to which president Trump replied

00:16:06.857 --> 00:16:08.237
"we're thinking about doing that.

00:16:08.237 --> 00:16:10.357
"It's one of the ways,
we have four or five ways

00:16:10.357 --> 00:16:12.677
"we can do it, it's one of
the ways we're thinking about

00:16:12.677 --> 00:16:14.052
"doing it very seriously.

00:16:14.052 --> 00:16:16.590
"We're doing well on the census."

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:18.620
So according to the president himself,

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.598
of course the citizenship
question was under consideration.

00:16:21.598 --> 00:16:24.000
It's hard to criticize the news media

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.620
for being hysterical when
they're simply reporting

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.720
what president Trump himself said.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:31.740
Now one of the consequences
of Barr and Trump's reversals

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:34.100
is that the DOJ lawyers
were thrown under the bus

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:35.510
in front of the federal courts.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:38.122
Rather than continue litigating this case,

00:16:38.122 --> 00:16:43.122
all of the DOJ lawyers asked
to be withdrawn from the case,

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:46.240
both in the Maryland case
and in the New York case,

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:49.270
which is basically an unprecedented move.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.650
It really hearkens back to

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:53.810
the Saturday night massacre under Nixon.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.570
The Department of
Justice would not say why

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:58.820
those lawyers asked to be
withdrawn from the case,

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.730
but it's safe to say that
some of them refused to

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:04.070
go back into court and
contradict their prior statements

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.636
to the judges, and to potentially defy

00:17:06.636 --> 00:17:08.850
the Supreme Court's precedent.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.560
The two federal judges who are overseeing

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.890
the various census cases were not amused

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:14.750
by this attempt to withdraw.

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.270
Judge Furman of the US District Court

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:18.280
for the southern district of New York

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.670
would not allow any of
the lawyers to withdraw

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.170
in the middle of the case, and stated that

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:25.170
the government's reasoning
to withdraw from the case

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.580
were patently deficient.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:28.380
Judge Furman also said
that the government itself

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.222
was responsible for making the case

00:17:30.222 --> 00:17:32.400
a time-sensitive emergency.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.650
Quote, as this court
observed many months ago,

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.760
this case has been
litigated on the premise

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.599
based in no small part on
defendants' own insistence

00:17:39.599 --> 00:17:42.400
that a speedy resolution
of plaintiffs' claims

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:45.430
is a matter of great private
and public importance.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.480
This all goes back to the
government's insistence

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.080
that the case needed to be
wrapped up by June 30th,

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:52.077
and that deadline had expired.

00:17:52.077 --> 00:17:55.270
In the end, Judge Furman
denied the motion to withdraw

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.240
for nine of the 11 lawyers.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.350
The two who were granted
leave had apparently

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.830
quit the Department of
Justice prior that decision.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.388
Judge Hazel in the Maryland
district federal court

00:18:05.388 --> 00:18:07.660
followed suit by refusing to allow

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.300
the government lawyers to withdraw.

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:11.330
Judge Hazel, who's the one that conducted

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.157
the emergency court conference,

00:18:13.157 --> 00:18:15.470
said that a change in counsel did not give

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:18.040
the government a do-over,
and that even if it added

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.700
new lawyers, the government
would still have to

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.740
answer for the statements it made before.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.580
Quote, a change in counsel does not create

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.910
a clean slate for a party to proceed

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.180
as if prior representations
made to the court

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:29.930
were not in fact made.

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:33.057
A new DOJ team will need to
be prepared to address these

00:18:33.057 --> 00:18:35.890
and other previous representations made by

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:38.570
the withdrawing attorneys
at the appropriate juncture.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:40.890
For the time being, it looks
like the administration

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.780
is indeed backing down and
respecting the Supreme Court

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.410
decision, however, the
house has voted to hold

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.640
Attorney General Barr and
commerce secretary Wilbur Ross

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.450
in contempt of Congress for their refusal

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:54.330
to turn over key documents that relate

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:56.220
to the Trump administration's attempt

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:58.870
to add the citizenship
question to the 2020 census.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:01.100
So this in fact may just be the beginning

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:05.860
of another potential
constitutional crisis and dispute.

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:07.750
Now it's unlikely that
Attorney General Barr

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.790
fooled anyone about
what the president said

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.880
or what the administration
was trying to do.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.733
He really could have
benefited from Sabaa Tahir's

